AltoReferralWhitelistAdapter::setPaymentTokenShareReceiver
├── when caller is not whitelisted
│   └── it should revert
└── when caller is whitelisted
    ├── when setting receiver to same address as current receiver
    │   └── it should revert
    ├── when setting receiver to different address
    │   ├── when current receiver is zero (initial set)
    │   │   ├── it should set payment token share receiver mapping
    │   │   └── it should emit PaymentTokenShareReceiverSet event
    │   └── when current receiver is non-zero (update)
    │       ├── it should update payment token share receiver mapping
    │       └── it should emit PaymentTokenShareReceiverSet event with new receiver
    ├── when setting receiver to zero address (reset)
    │   ├── when current receiver is not zero
    │   │   ├── it should set payment token share receiver mapping to zero
    │   │   └── it should emit PaymentTokenShareReceiverSet event with zero address
    │   └── when current receiver is already zero
    │       └── it should revert
    └── when multiple whitelisted addresses set receivers
        ├── it should set independent receiver mappings for each address
        └── it should emit PaymentTokenShareReceiverSet event for each address

